# The repository is the first safety layer: what may never be committed is refused
# here, before any review happens. Ignoring a tool's cache below is hygiene, not a
# technology decision — no ADR is implied by any line in this file.

# ── Secrets (CLAUDE.md: no secrets in git) ───────────────────────────────────
# Real keys live in .env at the repo root and are read ONLY inside lab/ scripts.
# The committed, key-less interface is .env.example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Audio & recordings (charter G10: recordings are ephemeral) ───────────────
# A child's voice is scored, then purged — it never enters git, in any folder.
# Lab audio (the developer's own voice, consented adults) stays local too.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.flac
*.webm
recordings/

# ── Lab outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Results live in each experiment's README table; raw outputs stay in out/,
# local. A small output worth sharing is added deliberately:
#   git add -f lab/<step-id>-<slug>/out/<file>
lab/*/out/
lab/*/.tmp/

# ── Docs pipeline scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# render-diagrams.py works in a .tmp/ folder beside the documents (0.6 gotcha).
docs/deliverables/.tmp/

# ── Tool caches & local environments ─────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# ── OS & editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
